abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 proof, accepted by two independent kernels (Lean's and nanoda) through Comparator in local, unsandboxed runs, that for squarefree m >= 1 the
  field Q(sqrt(-m)) has class number one if and only if m is in {1, 2, 3, 7, 11, 19, 43, 67, 163}. The proof uses no Heegner,
  Baker, Stark or Gross-Zagier input. It goes through OpenAI's zero-free region Re s > 7/8 for Dirichlet L-functions, whose Lean
  proof is inside the checked closure, and the Chowla-Selberg formula at s = 7/8, which gives the explicit bound d <= 652 proved
  in Lean, followed by kernel-checked split-prime witnesses for the finite range. Written for T. Tao's tenth-discriminant
  challenge (20 October 2026).
